Description: qmi: bind each bearer WDS client to the primary subscription
 On a multi-SIM (DSDS) Qualcomm modem an unbound WDS client follows the default
 data subscription (DDS). Nothing on Linux sets the DDS, and on the POCO X3 NFC
 (SM7150) it points at a subscription without a SIM: every connect fails at once
 with CallFailed, verbose call end reason (3,2001) [cm] no-service, while the
 modem is registered on LTE and PS-attached. Verified with a raw QMI client: an
 unbound or secondary-bound client gets no-service, a primary-bound one gets the
 call up. ModemManager only uses the primary GW session, so bind the IPv4 and
 IPv6 WDS clients to the primary subscription after Bind (Mux) Data Port (which
 resets the binding). Modems without the message keep the default, as before.
Author: VibeOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
